# Methods {#sec-methods}

The approach in one display equation:

$$ D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\,\|\,Q) = \sum_k p_k \log\frac{p_k}{q_k} $$ {#eq-kl}

The divergence is non-negative, with equality exactly when $P = Q$, so the objective in
@eq-kl is bounded below. Expanding the complex exponential with @eq-euler from the
previous chapter gives the oscillatory form we use in the appendix.

